1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,600
Equilibrium calculations stump a lot of students, and

2
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:05,200
it is rarely the algebra.

3
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:08,480
It is a small trap early on: moles

4
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,840
where K needs concentrations, a coefficient missed in

5
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:14,640
the change row, a solid left in K,

6
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:17,280
or a K written for the other equation.

7
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:20,720
Here are four HSC-style questions, and the last

8
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:22,280
one has two parts.

9
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:24,880
Each hides at least one trap.

10
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:27,600
Pause and try each one, then we'll work

11
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:29,360
it through one step at a time, and

12
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:30,960
look at the classic mistake.

13
00:00:32,167 --> 00:00:33,046
Question one.

14
00:00:33,607 --> 00:00:37,046
Iron two oxide, a solid, reacts with carbon

15
00:00:37,127 --> 00:00:40,486
monoxide to make solid iron and carbon dioxide.

16
00:00:41,047 --> 00:00:45,046
At about 800 degrees, K is 0.50.

17
00:00:45,767 --> 00:00:49,526
A sealed 2.00 litre vessel holds an excess

18
00:00:49,607 --> 00:00:53,446
of iron two oxide and 0.600 moles of

19
00:00:53,527 --> 00:00:57,046
carbon monoxide, with no iron or carbon dioxide

20
00:00:57,087 --> 00:00:57,766
at the start.

21
00:00:58,487 --> 00:01:01,766
What mass of iron is present at equilibrium?

22
00:01:01,927 --> 00:01:03,126
Pause here to answer.

23
00:01:13,534 --> 00:01:15,013
Start with the expression.

24
00:01:15,294 --> 00:01:18,333
Iron two oxide and iron are solids, so

25
00:01:18,494 --> 00:01:19,853
they stay out of K.

26
00:01:20,414 --> 00:01:23,533
That leaves K equals carbon dioxide over carbon

27
00:01:23,614 --> 00:01:25,853
monoxide, with no powers at all.

28
00:01:26,414 --> 00:01:28,813
Now the I C E table: I for

29
00:01:28,894 --> 00:01:32,333
initial, C for change, E for equilibrium.

30
00:01:32,894 --> 00:01:35,613
The carbon monoxide is in moles, so divide

31
00:01:35,694 --> 00:01:40,653
first: 0.600 over 2.00 is

32
00:01:40,734 --> 00:01:45,453
0.300 moles per litre, and carbon dioxide starts

33
00:01:45,494 --> 00:01:46,333
at zero.

34
00:01:46,654 --> 00:01:49,373
Nothing at equilibrium is measured, so the change

35
00:01:49,454 --> 00:01:54,413
is x: carbon monoxide ends at 0.300 minus

36
00:01:54,574 --> 00:01:57,213
x, and carbon dioxide at x.

37
00:01:58,434 --> 00:02:03,153
So x over 0.300 minus x equals

38
00:02:03,314 --> 00:02:05,153
0.50.

39
00:02:05,274 --> 00:02:07,713
K is not tiny, so do not drop

40
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:08,513
the x.

41
00:02:08,674 --> 00:02:10,913
You do not need to: this equation is

42
00:02:10,994 --> 00:02:12,233
already simple.

43
00:02:12,514 --> 00:02:16,913
Multiply both sides by the bottom, 0.300 minus

44
00:02:17,074 --> 00:02:23,233
x: x equals 0.150 minus 0.50 x.

45
00:02:23,474 --> 00:02:27,633
Add 0.50 x to both sides, so 1.50

46
00:02:27,714 --> 00:02:31,073
x is 0.150.

47
00:02:31,154 --> 00:02:34,993
Then divide both sides by 1.50, and x

48
00:02:35,074 --> 00:02:37,473
is 0.100.

49
00:02:37,674 --> 00:02:42,433
Check: 0.100 over 0.200 is

50
00:02:42,514 --> 00:02:44,033
0.50.

51
00:02:45,234 --> 00:02:47,273
But the question asks for a mass of

52
00:02:47,314 --> 00:02:47,793
iron.

53
00:02:48,194 --> 00:02:50,833
The equation makes one iron for every carbon

54
00:02:50,914 --> 00:02:54,193
dioxide, so the moles of iron formed equal

55
00:02:54,234 --> 00:02:56,273
the moles of carbon dioxide formed.

56
00:02:56,754 --> 00:03:01,633
That is 0.100 moles per litre, times 2.00

57
00:03:01,754 --> 00:03:06,313
litres, which is 0.200 moles.

58
00:03:06,594 --> 00:03:10,673
Times 55.85 grams per mole, that is 11.2

59
00:03:10,834 --> 00:03:12,433
grams of iron.

60
00:03:12,994 --> 00:03:15,953
The classic mistake is stopping at the concentration,

61
00:03:16,074 --> 00:03:19,633
or forgetting the volume and getting 5.6 grams.

62
00:03:20,834 --> 00:03:21,713
Question two.

63
00:03:22,354 --> 00:03:26,433
Carbon monoxide and hydrogen make methanol gas: C

64
00:03:26,514 --> 00:03:29,153
O plus two H two makes methanol.

65
00:03:29,714 --> 00:03:34,033
A 2.00 litre vessel at about 230 degrees

66
00:03:34,354 --> 00:03:39,553
starts with 0.200 moles of carbon monoxide, 0.400

67
00:03:39,634 --> 00:03:44,193
moles of hydrogen and 0.400 moles

68
00:03:44,274 --> 00:03:45,553
of methanol.

69
00:03:45,634 --> 00:03:50,393
At equilibrium, it holds 0.320 moles of methanol.

70
00:03:50,674 --> 00:03:51,953
Calculate K.

71
00:03:52,274 --> 00:03:53,553
Pause here to answer.

72
00:04:03,967 --> 00:04:07,246
Everything here is in moles, so first divide

73
00:04:07,327 --> 00:04:09,406
by 2.00.

74
00:04:09,447 --> 00:04:13,886
The initial row is 0.100 for carbon monoxide,

75
00:04:13,967 --> 00:04:18,526
0.200 for hydrogen and 0.200 for

76
00:04:18,607 --> 00:04:19,086
methanol.

77
00:04:19,487 --> 00:04:25,166
The measured methanol, 0.320 moles, is 0.160 moles

78
00:04:25,247 --> 00:04:27,646
per litre, and it goes in the equilibrium

79
00:04:27,727 --> 00:04:28,246
row.

80
00:04:28,527 --> 00:04:33,646
Change is equilibrium minus initial: 0.160 minus

81
00:04:33,727 --> 00:04:38,926
0.200 is minus 0.0400.

82
00:04:39,007 --> 00:04:42,486
Methanol went down, so this mixture ran backwards.

83
00:04:42,687 --> 00:04:44,366
You did not have to guess that: the

84
00:04:44,487 --> 00:04:46,206
subtraction gave you the sign.

85
00:04:47,434 --> 00:04:48,953
Now the coefficients.

86
00:04:49,274 --> 00:04:52,473
Each methanol that splits gives one carbon monoxide

87
00:04:52,634 --> 00:04:56,473
and two hydrogen, so carbon monoxide rises by

88
00:04:56,634 --> 00:05:03,753
0.0400 and hydrogen rises by 0.0800.

89
00:05:03,874 --> 00:05:06,953
Add each change to its start: carbon monoxide

90
00:05:07,354 --> 00:05:12,713
0.140, hydrogen 0.280.

91
00:05:12,914 --> 00:05:16,313
K is methanol over carbon monoxide times hydrogen

92
00:05:16,394 --> 00:05:17,433
squared.

93
00:05:17,554 --> 00:05:22,473
0.280 squared is 0.0784,

94
00:05:22,554 --> 00:05:28,873
and times 0.140 that is 0.01098.

95
00:05:28,954 --> 00:05:31,193
Keep the extra figures until the end.

96
00:05:31,314 --> 00:05:36,073
0.160 over 0.01098 gives

97
00:05:36,474 --> 00:05:38,713
K is 14.6.

98
00:05:39,934 --> 00:05:42,573
The classic mistake here is writing the measured

99
00:05:42,654 --> 00:05:46,293
0.160 straight into the change row.

100
00:05:46,574 --> 00:05:48,653
It is not a change, it is where

101
00:05:48,734 --> 00:05:50,173
methanol ended up.

102
00:05:50,494 --> 00:05:52,573
Put it in the equilibrium row, and let

103
00:05:52,694 --> 00:05:55,933
equilibrium minus initial give you the change, sign

104
00:05:56,014 --> 00:05:56,653
and all.

105
00:05:57,867 --> 00:05:59,026
Question three.

106
00:05:59,307 --> 00:06:02,026
For two N O plus chlorine making two

107
00:06:02,187 --> 00:06:05,786
N O C L, nitrosyl chloride, K is

108
00:06:05,907 --> 00:06:08,546
6.25 times ten to the four at a

109
00:06:08,587 --> 00:06:09,906
certain temperature.

110
00:06:10,347 --> 00:06:13,386
2.00 moles of N O C L is

111
00:06:13,547 --> 00:06:16,826
placed in an empty 4.00 litre vessel at

112
00:06:16,947 --> 00:06:19,546
that temperature, and some of it splits.

113
00:06:19,867 --> 00:06:22,026
How many moles of chlorine are present at

114
00:06:22,107 --> 00:06:22,826
equilibrium?

115
00:06:23,387 --> 00:06:24,746
Pause here to answer.

116
00:06:35,167 --> 00:06:37,486
Look at which way the equation runs.

117
00:06:37,727 --> 00:06:39,806
K was given for the equation that makes

118
00:06:39,967 --> 00:06:42,846
N O C L, but this vessel starts

119
00:06:42,927 --> 00:06:45,166
with N O C L, which splits.

120
00:06:45,487 --> 00:06:47,406
K belongs to the equation as it is

121
00:06:47,487 --> 00:06:49,966
written, so write the equation the way this

122
00:06:50,047 --> 00:06:52,926
vessel runs, and flip K with it: one

123
00:06:53,087 --> 00:06:56,046
over 6.25 times ten to the four is

124
00:06:56,127 --> 00:06:59,166
1.6 times ten to the minus five, which

125
00:06:59,247 --> 00:07:00,326
is tiny.

126
00:07:00,687 --> 00:07:03,326
Question two ran backwards too, but we kept

127
00:07:03,407 --> 00:07:05,806
its equation as given, so its K stayed

128
00:07:05,887 --> 00:07:07,006
the same.

129
00:07:07,127 --> 00:07:08,286
Now the table.

130
00:07:08,367 --> 00:07:13,486
The start is 2.00 over 4.00, 0.500

131
00:07:13,647 --> 00:07:16,126
moles per litre.

132
00:07:16,247 --> 00:07:18,926
If x of chlorine forms, then two x

133
00:07:18,967 --> 00:07:21,006
of N O C L splits and two

134
00:07:21,087 --> 00:07:23,806
x of N O forms, so the equilibrium

135
00:07:23,887 --> 00:07:28,606
row is 0.500 minus two x, two x,

136
00:07:28,687 --> 00:07:29,406
and x.

137
00:07:30,634 --> 00:07:33,913
K is two x all squared, times x,

138
00:07:34,234 --> 00:07:38,953
over 0.500 minus two x, all squared.

139
00:07:39,074 --> 00:07:42,393
K is tiny, so very little splits: drop

140
00:07:42,474 --> 00:07:44,073
the two x from the bottom, and keep

141
00:07:44,154 --> 00:07:45,993
the x on top, because that is the

142
00:07:46,074 --> 00:07:47,113
answer.

143
00:07:47,194 --> 00:07:53,113
The bottom becomes 0.500 squared, 0.250.

144
00:07:53,194 --> 00:07:56,473
On top, two x all squared, times x,

145
00:07:56,554 --> 00:07:58,313
is four x cubed.

146
00:07:58,554 --> 00:08:02,793
Multiply both sides by the bottom, 0.250: four

147
00:08:02,874 --> 00:08:05,593
x cubed is 4.0 times ten to the

148
00:08:05,674 --> 00:08:07,033
minus six.

149
00:08:07,154 --> 00:08:10,233
Then divide both sides by four: x cubed

150
00:08:10,314 --> 00:08:13,193
is 1.0 times ten to the minus six,

151
00:08:13,314 --> 00:08:16,553
and x is 0.0100.

152
00:08:17,767 --> 00:08:18,886
Check the shortcut.

153
00:08:19,287 --> 00:08:21,446
The amount taken off the start is two

154
00:08:21,527 --> 00:08:26,166
x, not x: 0.0200 out of

155
00:08:26,247 --> 00:08:29,686
0.500 is 4 per cent.

156
00:08:29,767 --> 00:08:32,726
That is under about 5, so it passes,

157
00:08:32,807 --> 00:08:34,086
but only just.

158
00:08:34,647 --> 00:08:39,286
Chlorine is 0.0100 moles per litre, times 4.00

159
00:08:39,367 --> 00:08:44,486
litres, which is 0.0400 moles.

160
00:08:44,567 --> 00:08:47,686
The classic mistake is putting 6.25 times ten

161
00:08:47,767 --> 00:08:50,326
to the four into the splitting expression without

162
00:08:50,407 --> 00:08:51,446
flipping it.

163
00:08:51,527 --> 00:08:53,686
That gives x of about 16 moles per

164
00:08:53,807 --> 00:08:57,526
litre, far more than the 0.500 you started

165
00:08:57,607 --> 00:08:59,206
with, which is impossible.

166
00:09:00,434 --> 00:09:02,433
Question four has two parts.

167
00:09:03,074 --> 00:09:06,593
Nitrogen dioxide and sulfur dioxide react to make

168
00:09:06,674 --> 00:09:10,993
nitrogen monoxide and sulfur trioxide, all gases.

169
00:09:11,314 --> 00:09:15,793
At 460 degrees, a 5.00 litre vessel at

170
00:09:15,874 --> 00:09:20,833
equilibrium holds 0.100 moles of N O two,

171
00:09:20,954 --> 00:09:25,873
0.200 of S O two, 0.900 of

172
00:09:25,954 --> 00:09:29,673
N O and 1.80 of S O three.

173
00:09:30,034 --> 00:09:32,393
Part a: calculate K.

174
00:09:32,674 --> 00:09:33,953
Pause here to answer.

175
00:09:44,367 --> 00:09:50,606
Divide each amount by 5.00: 0.0200,

176
00:09:50,727 --> 00:09:55,326
0.0400, 0.180 and

177
00:09:55,447 --> 00:09:58,366
0.360 moles per litre.

178
00:09:58,927 --> 00:10:02,286
Every coefficient is one, so K is N

179
00:10:02,367 --> 00:10:05,006
O times S O three, over N O

180
00:10:05,087 --> 00:10:06,726
two times S O two.

181
00:10:07,007 --> 00:10:11,806
On top, 0.180 times 0.360 is

182
00:10:11,927 --> 00:10:14,366
0.0648.

183
00:10:14,447 --> 00:10:20,606
Underneath, 0.0200 times 0.0400 is

184
00:10:20,727 --> 00:10:24,126
0.000800.

185
00:10:24,247 --> 00:10:26,846
So K is 81.0.

186
00:10:28,067 --> 00:10:29,146
Part b.

187
00:10:29,427 --> 00:10:33,426
At the same temperature, 0.500 moles of N

188
00:10:33,507 --> 00:10:37,346
O two and 0.500 moles of S O

189
00:10:37,467 --> 00:10:40,866
two are placed in an empty 2.00 litre

190
00:10:40,947 --> 00:10:41,986
vessel.

191
00:10:42,107 --> 00:10:44,146
Find the concentration of N O two at

192
00:10:44,227 --> 00:10:45,506
equilibrium.

193
00:10:45,667 --> 00:10:46,866
Pause here to answer.

194
00:10:57,267 --> 00:11:01,346
Same temperature, so the same K: 81.0 from

195
00:11:01,427 --> 00:11:02,346
part a.

196
00:11:02,627 --> 00:11:06,306
The start is 0.250 of each reactant.

197
00:11:06,867 --> 00:11:09,586
Each reactant changes by minus x, and each

198
00:11:09,747 --> 00:11:11,186
product by plus x.

199
00:11:11,747 --> 00:11:15,026
So K is x times x, over 0.250

200
00:11:15,107 --> 00:11:19,746
minus x, times 0.250 minus x.

201
00:11:20,307 --> 00:11:22,626
That looks like it needs the quadratic formula.

202
00:11:23,027 --> 00:11:24,546
You can use it if you like, but

203
00:11:24,627 --> 00:11:27,106
HSC questions are written so you shouldn't need

204
00:11:27,187 --> 00:11:28,386
it, so look again.

205
00:11:28,867 --> 00:11:31,346
The top is x squared, and the bottom

206
00:11:31,507 --> 00:11:34,946
is 0.250 minus x, all squared.

207
00:11:35,507 --> 00:11:37,426
It is a perfect square, because the two

208
00:11:37,507 --> 00:11:39,186
reactants started equal.

209
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:43,200
Take the square root of both sides: x

210
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:48,080
over 0.250 minus x is 9.00.

211
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:52,720
Multiply both sides by the bottom, 0.250 minus

212
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:57,200
x: x equals 2.25 minus 9 x.

213
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:59,920
Add 9 x to both sides, so ten

214
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:04,320
x is 2.25, then divide by ten: x

215
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:06,520
is 0.225.

216
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:09,200
But the question asks for N O two,

217
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:15,280
which is 0.250 minus x: 0.0250 moles

218
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:15,920
per litre.

219
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:21,840
Check: 0.225 squared over 0.0250 squared

220
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,280
is 81.

221
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:25,760
The classic mistake is stopping at x and

222
00:12:25,840 --> 00:12:28,800
giving 0.225 as the answer.

223
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:31,040
x is the change, not the N O

224
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:31,600
two.

225
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:34,400
So here is what to look for.

226
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:37,960
Moles and a volume: divide first.

227
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:41,360
One equilibrium value: it goes in the equilibrium

228
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:44,880
row, and equilibrium minus initial gives the change

229
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:46,080
and its sign.

230
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:48,960
A coefficient: the change row follows it.

231
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:52,080
A solid, or water as the solvent: leave

232
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:53,120
it out of K.

233
00:12:53,520 --> 00:12:56,000
K for a different equation: flip it if

234
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:58,480
the equation is reversed, square it if it

235
00:12:58,560 --> 00:12:59,120
is doubled.

236
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:01,920
K and a start: look for a perfect

237
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,400
square, or a tiny K with the 5

238
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:06,320
per cent check on the amount taken off.

239
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:09,520
Asked for moles or grams: convert back at

240
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:10,080
the end.

241
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:12,800
And two parts at the same temperature use

242
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:13,760
the same K.

243
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:16,880
Next: how temperature changes K.

244
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:19,540
Here are the key notes.

